# Scenario: the first dungeon's boss (SCENARIO=dungeon1_boss), along the
# owner's boss session. Exploratory: run with DOTHEROES_DEV_CANT_DIE=1 to find
# the way, then without.
#
# Starts from: build/checkpoints/dungeon1-boss-door (CONTINUE: the Grass
#   Temple's entrance, the doors a test opened kept; the switches done).
# Route: the owner's boss session (build/sessions/boot-20261103-135259-
#   owner-boss, record 97-339 s; tests/route_from_record.py --buttons, menu
#   presses dropped), a fight on entering each room (25.6 x 19.2 cells): the
#   east room, its north door, the north-east rooms, back west to the room
#   north of the north room for the special key's chest (mark 1), the three
#   blocks, the six-pillar room, west and north to the portal room (its floor
#   plates) and the boss's door; then the boss (area 38).
# Completed when: area 38 reached and its fight segment ends.
# State (2026-11-03): boss1 followed the route to the key's room, but the chest
#   did not open from the owner's spot (no message): whatever makes it appear
#   (the room's enemies, an order of rooms) is not reproduced yet. The boss
#   itself is measured from the owner's session instead.
#! saves build/checkpoints/dungeon1-boss-door
